      "name": "AL26-026 - Critical vulnerabilities impacting PHP - CVE-2026-109618 and CVE-2026-109619 - Update 2",
      "description": "Known as \u201cphp2shell\u201d Footnote 6 , successful exploitation could allow an unauthenticated threat actor to execute arbitrary code on an affected system. Successful exploitation of CVE-2026-115560 requires an uncommon combination of PHP configuration and application behaviour. On October 26, 2026, Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Security Agency (CISA) added CVE-2026-109618 Footnote 11 and CVE-2026-109619 Footnote 12 to their Known Exploited Vulnerabilities (KEV) Database.",
